 .B \-\-bar\-total\-width
 The total width of the bar. Can be an expression.
 
+.TP
+.B \-\-box\-indicator
+Replaces the usual ring indicator with a password box: a rounded rectangle
+holding one dot per byte of input, which shakes when the password is wrong.
+Unlike the ring, the box is drawn whether or not anything has been typed yet.
+It is positioned with \-\-ind\-pos, and it takes its border from the
+\-\-ring\-color family and its fill from the \-\-inside\-color family, so an
+existing ring palette carries over unchanged.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-box\-width=number
+The width of the box, in pixels. Defaults to 340.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-box\-height=number
+The height of the box, in pixels. Defaults to 56.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-box\-radius=number
+The corner radius of the box. Defaults to 10. Clamped to half the shorter side,
+so a large value gives a stadium rather than an error.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-box\-border\-width=number
+The width of the box border. Defaults to 2. Note that this is separate from
+\-\-ring\-width, whose default of 7 is far too heavy for a rectangle.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-box\-dot\-radius=number
+The radius of each input dot. Defaults to 4.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-box\-dot\-gap=number
+The gap between input dots. Defaults to 10.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-box\-dot\-color=rrggbbaa
+The color of the input dots. Defaults to dadadaff.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-shake\-amplitude=number
+Peak horizontal travel of the shake, in pixels, before decay is applied.
+Defaults to 14.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-shake\-frequency=number
+Frequency of the shake, in Hz. Defaults to 13.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-shake\-duration=seconds\-as\-double
+How long the shake lasts. Defaults to 0.45. Set to 0 to keep the box but
+disable the movement.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-lockout\-after=number
+Rate limit after this many consecutive failed attempts. Every further attempt
+then costs \-\-lockout\-delay seconds before it will be looked at, and the
+indicator shows a countdown. Defaults to 0, which disables it.
+.IP
