+keyboard guessing; it does nothing about an attacker who can power-cycle the
+machine, because the counter lives in the running locker and a fresh one starts
+at zero. Note also that it is not
+.BR pam_faillock (8):
+no PAM state is touched, so this can never lock you out of sudo or a TTY. The
+worst it can do is make you wait.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-lockout\-delay=seconds\-as\-double
+How long each attempt costs once the limit is in force. Defaults to 30.
+
+.TP
+.B \-\-lockout\-text=string
+Prefix shown with the countdown, rendered as "<text> <n>s". Defaults to "wait".
+Taken literally: a percent sign in here is printed, not interpreted as a format.
+
